NAME

ulibScanFidoNetConfig - Obtain configured information on a FidoNet node.


SYNOPSIS

UBYTE ulibScanFidoNetConfig(struct FidoNetConfigCmd *Cmd)
                                       a0


DESCRIPTION

This function obtains configured information on a specified FidoNet node, by
reading the SYSTEMS.XLK data file.

The information returned by this function includes the session password,
preferred archive type, and linkup protocol preference.

The <Cmd->Fido> field must specify a FidoNet address, and all other fields
must be zeroed prior to calling this function.

If the function is successful, the session password will be filled out in
the <Cmd->Password> field (if there is no session password, or the session
password was specified as "NONE", then <Cmd->Password> will be a null string),
the linkup protocol preference will be filled out in <Cmd->ConnectType>, and
the three letter preferred archive type abbreviation will be stored in
<Cmd->ArcType>.

The linkup protocol preference will be one of:

   CONNECT_UNKNOWN
   CONNECT_FTSC
   CONNECT_YOOHOO
   CONNECT_EMSI


RETURNS

0        - Success
Non-zero - Failure

   1     - Cannot open SYSTEMS.XLK
   2     - Insufficient memory to read SYSTEMS.XLK
   3     - System not found in file
